      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This isnt something that can be done by vrchat, its something that has to be done by the avatar creator. Vrchat has no way of knowing what animations count as \"expressions\", and the parameter that controls your expressions in this case (GestureLeft and GestureRight) also control your hand animations (and can also control other things like props, contact based interactions, and honestly anything you want). The best solution vrchat as a game can offer is disabling your controllers from inputting to the gesture parameters, which is what disabling your gestures does. If you want to take pictures with the hand animations playing but not the facial animations, i suggest either taking two photos and stitching them together (one with the gesture you want, and one with the expression you want), or contacting the avatar creator and asking them to add this feature.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
