      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64320355debe2a09d344abff|full_name} ^ is correct. All you need on your avatar for this is a boolean toggle to disable facial expressions, which will continue to allow updates to hand/finger-positions. If you have access to your avatar-files, you can just add an additional requirement (condition) for the transitions that cause facial-animation states to change. Something like facialExpressions = true.\n\nI'll note that because of the way inputs work for Index controllers, disabling Gestures from VRChat's Action (radial) menu will still allow fingers to move without driving facial expressions.",
